[recv] {"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"agentMessage","id":"msg_075d278199b58a94016a21afec2050819884c62ec00878814b","text":"Implemented a minimal tscircuit RP2040 schematic project in `/workspace`.\n\nCreated:\n- [index.circuit.tsx](/workspace/index.circuit.tsx)\n- [package.json](/workspace/package.json)\n- [tsconfig.json](/workspace/tsconfig.json)\n- Generated build output at [dist/index/circuit.json](/workspace/dist/index/circuit.json)\n\nWhat it includes:\n- RP2040 primitive `chip` with `qfn56` footprint\n- USB-C primitive connector footprint\n- 3.3 V regulator, decoupling, USB series resistors, CC pulldowns\n- QSPI flash, 12 MHz crystal, boot/reset buttons\n- SWD and GPIO headers\n- `routingDisabled` on the board\n- No tscircuit registry components used\n\nVerification run:\n- `npm run typecheck` passed\n- `npm run check:schematic` passed with no placement issues\n- `npm run build` completed and wrote `dist/index/circuit.json`\n\nBuild still emits non-blocking DRC/manufacturing warnings about generic footprints, missing `pinAttributes`, connector orientation, and one courtyard overlap. I left those because this was scoped as a schematic-agent test, not a production PCB layout pass.\n\n**TSCircuit Developer Feedback**\n- Confusing/surprising: `supplierPartNumbers.jlcpcb` must be an array, and generic footprints with JLC SKUs trigger footprint mismatch warnings even after the schematic is otherwise valid.\n- Most time wasted: resolving conflicting schematic-placement guidance for a dense RP2040 symbol; full 56-pin symbols can cause repeated width/height suggestions that fight label-collision checks.\n- Helpful improvements: clearer docs for compact schematic symbols, hiding pins from schematic arrangement, and valid footprint string lists.\n- Friction points: `tscircuit/jsx-runtime` was not exported despite the modern JSX config being the obvious setup; classic React JSX plus `import type {} from \"tscircuit\"` was needed.","phase":"final_answer","memoryCitation":null},"threadId":"019e938c-1a61-7d82-97d8-f72d6739dcf5","turnId":"019e938c-1a82-7fc0-99de-310ab0cf5af9","completedAtMs":1780592627535}}
